  <description>
    <p>
      Zalo is an unofficial, independent desktop client that loads the official
      Zalo Web interface in the system WebKitGTK webview. It is not affiliated
      with, endorsed by, or sponsored by VNG Corporation or Zalo.
    </p>
    <p>It adds desktop features beyond a browser tab:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Multiple isolated Zalo accounts in separate windows</li>
      <li>Native notifications, system tray integration, and close to tray</li>
      <li>Drag-and-drop attachment routing with bounded memory use</li>
      <li>Optional password lock and automatic idle locking</li>
      <li>Persistent sessions, display scaling, and configurable shortcuts</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Voice messages work on Linux. Voice and video calls normally do not because
      mainstream Linux WebKitGTK runtimes are built without compatible WebRTC support.
    </p>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.o365serveronms.zalors.desktop</launchable>

  <requires>
    <internet>always</internet>
    <display_length compare="ge">600</display_length>
  </requires>

  <recommends>
    <control>keyboard</control>
    <control>pointing</control>
  </recommends>

